<p>Former US President Barack Obama condemned what he called a breakdown of “shame” and “decorum” in American politics after a video shared on President Trump’s Truth Social account briefly showed Barack and Michelle Obama with their faces on monkeys’ bodies, according to reports. Obama made the comments in a wide-ranging interview released Saturday with political commentator Brian Tyler Cohen. The monkey depiction appeared inside a longer video promoting conspiracy claims about the 2020 election and drew widespread condemnation. The White House first dismissed the backlash as “fake outrage,” then said a staff mistake led to the post, which was removed.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TKhsClv0zYIghv05y8tDPAKu-P93IiePZJglPDbHoJbB1SYfIgRj_zVQ9LIW0Bhs4TNUdQTm5Xx0zDMpuGuDnNESfWBm20wncRX-TbW22QZr' alt='Former US President Barack Obama. — AFP/File' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Interview framing: Cohen pointed to the Truth Social post as an example of political discourse “devolv” into cruelty, telling Obama that “Just days ago” Trump shared an image putting Obama’s face on an ape’s body.</li><li>Immigration comment: In the same interview, Obama compared actions by agents enforcing the administration’s immigration crackdown in Minnesota to dictatorships, according to Dawn.</li><li>Video context: The monkey depiction appeared near the end of a roughly one-minute video promoting conspiracies about Trump’s 2020 election loss to Joe Biden, and it flashed on screen only briefly, the reports say.</li></ul><blockquote>There’s this sort of clown show that’s happening in social media and on television, and what is true is that there doesn’t seem to be any shame about this among people who used to feel like you had to have some sort of decorum and a sense of propriety and respect for the office, right? That’s been lost. - Barack Obama</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Barack Obama: Obama said many Americans find this kind of conduct “deeply troubling” and argued that expectations of propriety and respect for public office have eroded. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c74754j7qwgo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>White House: The White House shifted from calling the criticism “fake outrage” to saying the post was a staff error; it later removed the post, according to SCMP. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3343605/barack-obama-blasts-clown-show-after-trumps-racist-monkey-video'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Brian Tyler Cohen: Cohen pressed Obama on how the country can recover after the discourse “devolved,” using the Trump-shared monkey/ape depiction as a concrete example in the interview. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973370/obama-deplores-lack-of-shame-after-trumps-racist-monkey-clip'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1973370/obama-deplores-lack-of-shame-after-trumps-racist-monkey-clip'>Obama deplores lack of shame after Trump’s racist monkey clip</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3343605/barack-obama-blasts-clown-show-after-trumps-racist-monkey-video'>Barack Obama blasts ‘clown show’ after Trump’s racist monkey video</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/obama-deplores-lack-of-shame-after-trump-racist-social-media-post/article70634626.ece'>Obama deplores lack of shame after Trump racist social media post</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1r4x33w/obama_responds_to_trumps_video_of_him_and/'>Obama responds to Trump’s video of him and Michelle as apes and says MAGA lacks a sense of ‘shame’</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c74754j7qwgo'>Obama addresses racist video shared by Trump depicting him as an ape</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>